### Specific Areas for Improvement:  
- Add functionality to `main.py` for handling `do_POST`, which is crucial for user registration and login functionality.  
- Clearly define how blog posts will be retrieved and displayed in `templates/main_blog.html`, especially regarding error handling for empty states or no available posts.  
- Explicitly integrate error handling and user messaging into tasks, such as displaying messages when a post is successfully created or if a registration/login fails.  
- Identify dependencies more clearly between tasks, particularly ensuring user authentication is implemented before allowing any post management operations.  
- Break down tasks regarding user authentication (registration/login) and blog post management (creation, editing, deleting, viewing) into distinct sub-tasks for clarity and improved workflow.

### Suggested Enhancements:  
- Prioritize the completion of user authentication tasks (registration and login) to establish foundational access before progressing to post management tasks.  
- Provide additional clarity on form functionality and expected behaviors after user actions in templates, detailing validation requirements and expected user feedback for both successful and erroneous submissions.  
- Enhance specifications for post management to clarify what metadata (e.g., author names, timestamps) should be included and how edit functionality will communicate success or failure to the user.  
- Group tasks strategically according to related functionalities (e.g., user authentication vs. post management) for better organization and understanding of workflows.  
- Include provisions for handling cases where users attempt to access features without proper authentication, maintaining a seamless user experience.
